cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use readsync, please cite the version you used."
type: software
title: "readsync: a toolkit for synchronised reading experiments with eye-tracking and EEG"
abstract: >-
  A Python toolkit for reading experiments that record eye movements and, optionally,
  EEG. It presents annotated reading materials, derives word interest areas, sends
  event markers to the eye-tracker's data file and to the EEG recording and keeps an
  encrypted, tamper-evident session log. The code is released under the MIT Licence.
  The bundled stimulus files are released under CC BY-SA 4.0, because their Zipf
  values come from wordfreq's data. Their sentences, passages and questions are also
  released on their own under CC BY 4.0.
authors:
